        "math_academy_id": "q-17317",
        "knowledge_point_id": "57987f7d-21e1-51cb-a745-a24f2b257f11",
        "knowledge_point": "Finding All the Roots of a Quartic Equation Given Two Real Roots",
        "problem": "Given that $x=-1$ and $x=4$ are solutions to the equation ${x}^{4}-3{x}^{3}-12x-16=0,$ find the remaining solutions.",
        "worked_solution": "Let $f(x)={x}^{4}-3{x}^{3}-12x-16.$ Since ${x}_{1}=-1$ and ${x}_{2}=4$ are roots of $f(x),$ then according to the factor theorem, \n\n$$\n(x+1)(x-4)={x}^{2}-3x-4\n$$\n\nis a factor of $f(x).$ \n\nNext, we find the quotient when $f(x)$ is divided by ${x}^{2}-3x-4$ using polynomial division.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{x}^{2}+4 \\\\  & {x}^{2}-3x-4\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,{x}^{4}-3{x}^{3}\\phantom{+0x}\\,\\,\\,-12x-16\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{{x}^{4}-3{x}^{3}-4{x}^{2}}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,4{x}^{2}-12x-16 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{4{x}^{2}-12x-16}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, $f(x)=({x}^{2}-3x-4)({x}^{2}+4).$\n\nTo find the remaining two roots, we solve ${x}^{2}+4=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+4 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =-4 \\\\ x & =\\pm 2\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solutions to our original equation are $x=-1,\\,4,\\,\\pm 2\\text{i}.$",
